Snapshot of commit `{{ short }}`.

**Linux** (x86_64, glibc 2.35 or newer)

    curl -fLO {{ release_url }}/{{ linux }}

**macOS, Apple Silicon**

    curl -fLO {{ release_url }}/{{ mac_arm }}

**macOS, Intel**

    curl -fLO {{ release_url }}/{{ mac_intel }}

**macOS app, Apple Silicon** (the Homebrew cask installs this)

    curl -fLO {{ release_url }}/{{ app_arm }}

**macOS app, Intel** (the Homebrew cask installs this)

    curl -fLO {{ release_url }}/{{ app_intel }}

The app bundles are what `rikardg/tap/noido-snapshot`
installs; the cask's updater reads their names from this
page.

Use `curl` to avoid the download being quarantined on macOS, or clear the quarantine attribute with:

    xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine noido-*.tar.gz

Unpack and (optionally) copy out noido to a directory that is in PATH. Then run `noido --install` to integrate it with the system launcher.

